      "message": "Other hypercalls, unlike set_msr, take the host\u0027s values as is, don\u0027t validate them... OTOH, after a closer look, it may be still problematic to allow the host to change these values while pKVM is using them. For example, looking at this logic in __vmx_set_segment():\n```\n                vmx-\u003ermode.segs[seg] \u003d *var;\n                if (seg \u003d\u003d VCPU_SREG_TR)\n                        vmcs_write16(sf-\u003eselector, var-\u003eselector);\n                else if (var-\u003es)\n                        fix_rmode_seg(seg, \u0026vmx-\u003ermode.segs[seg]);\n```\n\nSo generally it would be probably indeed better to address this generically (e.g. something like what Vineeth suggested: throw away this_pv_param() and instead provide macros for getting/setting pv_param value to/from a local variable).",
